There are documents entitled Solved Exams under Files.

These are all a and b problems from previous exams worked out by some stude=
nt. One's a nd b problems will be different. One will have to do the c prob=
lems by oneself. Solved problems for the Problem Set will not be provided.

The J numbers for the Solved Exams are fictitious.

The syntax and formatting on these exams are exactly correct.

One should follow the same arrangement and organisation, putting things in =
exactly the same relative positions, drawing all straight line segments wit=
h rulers to make them visibly straight, and indexing them exactly as indica=
ted. Do not add ANY EXTRA SYMBOL or extraneous mark. Please fill in the top=
 sheet exactly as in the Solved Exam. One's expected score may not differ f=
rom the total score because one is supposed to prove that one's result is c=
orrect. One may not include work that one is not certain of. One may not in=
clude pages on which one does not attempt anything. Do not include blank sh=
eets. Points will be deducted for ANY DEPARTURE WHATSOEVER.

I HAVE DELIBERATELY NOT GRADED THE SOLUTIONS BECAUSE I WANT EVERY ONE TO RE=
AD THEM AND DECIDE IF THE SOLUTIONS ARE CORRECT.

The following are words from the student who produced these:

"Hardware:
A writing/drawing tablet. The cheapest options seem to start from around 40=
 bucks on Amazon (I think one should try to avoid making Bezos richer).

Software:

Krita: Krita is a free and open source painting program. It mainly uses ras=
ter graphics. This is where I do all my writing work. I import PDFs into Kr=
ita, write all that I want to, then render separate images for separate pag=
es.

Better software to do these exams might exist, but I haven't looked for suc=
h software yet, since Krita gets the job done for me."



One may always write by hand on unruled paper and then scan them. Many have=
 done so very well.

The purpose of this announcement is to make one aware of these matters.

