/span></p>
<p>The following are words from the student who produced these:<br>
<br>
<strong>&quot;Hardware:</strong><br>
<strong>A writing/drawing tablet. The cheapest options seem to start from a=
round 40 bucks on Amazon (I think one should try to avoid making Bezos rich=
er).</strong><br>
<br>
<strong>Software:</strong></p>
<p><strong>Krita: Krita is a free and open source painting program. It main=
ly uses raster graphics. This is where I do all my writing work. I import P=
DFs into Krita, write all that I want to, then render separate images for s=
eparate pages.</strong><br>
<br>
<strong>Better software to do these exams might exist, but I haven't looked=
 for such software yet, since Krita gets the job done for me.&quot;</strong=
></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>One may always write by hand on unruled paper and then scan them. Many h=
